                TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST := 3;
            ELSE
                TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST := 2;
            END_IF;
        END_IF;
```

For the auto mode, I need to determine the setpoint based on occupancy and energy saving settings. When the space is unoccupied, energy saving mode applies a higher offset of 3°C compared to 2°C in standard mode. The other modes (comfort and economy) follow similar logic with their respective temperature adjustments.

